INSERT INTO mono_blocks VALUES ('86984142-5f1a-4018-af62-ddb105cb6cb4', 2636, '{"role": "tool", "text": "M=''/Applications/MonoCode 2.app/Contents/MacOS/monocode''; \"$M\" app sessions.send --json ''{\"sessionId\":\"app-86984142-5f1a-4018-af62-ddb105cb6cb4-b4677bea-0d5c-4efe-b570-6a3d7a1eab69\",\"notifyOnComplete\":true,\"prompt\":\"Two fix rounds, do them in this order. Work in poteto-mode. No git stash. Skip project-wide formatters. Finish ping with --json exactly as common.md shows.\\n\\n1) #139 R4, review round 2 (change-r/reviews/r4-round2.md): 0B/0M/1m. The save-wait for sessions.start workers has no test: limiting the wait to /operator turns still passes the e7 spec. Add one e7 Playwright case: a lead starts a worker, saving that worker fails, and the worker gets no prompt. Show that limiting the wait to /operator now fails it. Nits n6-n10 stay in #140. Review rounds: 2. Push, wait for CI, reply on the App.tsx:8232 line comment, do not merge (the merge also waits on Tyler waiving the 2 new strings).\\n\\n2) #142 R3, review round 1 (change-r/reviews/r3-round1.md): 0B/1M/4m. M1: wait_for in app.sh:31 never waits on macOS (the ^(0|)$ regex does not compile, exit 2 is read as done). Make it a real wait with a timeout that fails, delete the fixed sleep 5, and prove the timeout path runs (a probe that never becomes true fails after the timeout). m1: run the /tmp guard before the first write, and make run_s0 fail closed (no || that turns off set -e). m2: make the puppet answer the fx detection on purpose (handle --help / the detection input explicitly), not through a comment. m3: replace sample()-then-four-reads with one method that returns all four values. m4: add a CI job (or a step) that builds with --features fake-clock. Re-run S0 through the real app 3 times on a GigaEval folder only. Nits in #149. Keep it near 400 non-test; if the fixes push it well over, split and say how. Review rounds: 1. Push, wait for CI, reply on the line comments, do not merge.\\n\\nReport both new heads, CI, and the proof for each.\"}'' | jq -c ''{ok,error}''", "tool": {"detail": "{\"ok\":true,\"error\":null}\n\n\nWall time: 0.10 seconds"}}', 0);
